  "subtitle": "Five visitors to a haunted house",
  "summary": "Sweet Home is Capcom’s Famicom role-playing game about a documentary crew trapped inside a haunted mansion. The five visitors arrive to recover and photograph valuable frescoes, then discover that leaving will require more than finding the front door. Developed alongside the Japanese horror film of the same name, it combines a connected building, supernatural encounters and limited supplies. The player manages the whole group rather than a single hero, making each person’s survival part of the practical problem of exploring the house.",
  "body": [
    "Sweet Home is Capcom’s Famicom role-playing game about a documentary crew trapped inside a haunted mansion. The five visitors arrive to recover and photograph valuable frescoes, then discover that leaving will require more than finding the front door. Developed alongside the Japanese horror film of the same name, it combines a connected building, supernatural encounters and limited supplies. The player manages the whole group rather than a single hero, making each person’s survival part of the practical problem of exploring the house.",
    "Each crew member carries a particular tool, including a camera, lighter, medical kit, lockpick or vacuum cleaner. Characters can explore alone or in small parties, and the player can switch between those groups. An item found in one place may be left for somebody else to collect, so the mansion becomes a shared space to organise. Random battles interrupt that work, while scarce healing supplies make each encounter matter. Reaching a blocked passage often means reconsidering who is nearby and what that person can carry.",
    "A dead character stays dead, but the adventure continues. Replacement items can provide a lost tool’s function, allowing the remaining crew to progress with fewer people. Notes and messages help explain the mansion while also supplying clues, connecting its story to the search for a route through it. Different endings reflect how many characters survive. Sweet Home later provided a major point of reference for Resident Evil, particularly its concern with a dangerous building, restricted inventories and the consequences of deciding how to use limited resources."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "Five visitors to a haunted house",
    "The right person for the room",
    "What remains after a loss"
  ],
